  "finding": "These editions retain the same internal model identities, material names, scripts and animations while supplying different local texture bytes. This is a concrete historical example of manual per-installation texture editions, not automatic renderer switching inside one GOB.",
  "limits": [
    "Archive identity supports the proposed same-model-name mechanism but is not a newly executed original-JK multiplayer compatibility test.",
    "The complete GOBs are not a MAT-only delta: eight bitmap payloads and one text payload also differ, and the 16-bit edition has nine additional MATs.",
    "Absence from supplied 3DO material lists does not prove the nine extra MATs are unused by every other resource.",
    "Installing both overlapping editions simultaneously would involve resource precedence; this audit does not establish an automatic choice by renderer.",
    "This selected historical example does not establish that every past skin used the same approach or that a peer without the package will be compatible."
  ]
